    {
      "id": "2105544504535396482",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-01T06:25:03.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-01 14:25:03",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Data centers on the ground are limited by permits and power.\n\nSpaceX's answer is Starmind, orbital AI data centers with about 72 Nvidia chips and up to 175 kW per satellite.\n\nThat's about 5,700 satellites per gigawatt. Terafab builds the chips, and Starship launches them.\n\n@JOBhakdi thinks it goes from gigawatts to terawatts by 2028 or 2029.\n\n$SPCX",
